2026-10-20T15:22:00.4760290Z [34m==>[0m [1mphp@8.4[0m
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4761680Z To enable PHP in Apache add the following to httpd.conf and restart Apache:
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4763340Z     LoadModule php_module /opt/homebrew/opt/php@8.4/lib/httpd/modules/libphp.so
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4764130Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4764410Z     <FilesMatch \.php$>
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4765140Z         SetHandler application/x-httpd-php
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4766140Z     </FilesMatch>
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4766500Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4767140Z Finally, check DirectoryIndex includes index.php
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4775750Z     DirectoryIndex index.php index.html
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4776240Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4776570Z The php.ini and php-fpm.ini file can be found in:
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4777060Z     /opt/homebrew/etc/php/8.4/
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4777270Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4777610Z To start php@8.4 now and restart at login:
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4777980Z   brew services start php@8.4
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4778580Z Or, if you don't want/need a background service you can just run:
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4779240Z   /opt/homebrew/opt/php@8.4/sbin/php-fpm --nodaemonize
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4779990Z [34m==>[0m [1mllvm[0m
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4780480Z CLANG_CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_DIR: /opt/homebrew/etc/clang
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4781030Z CLANG_CONFIG_FILE_USER_DIR:   ~/.config/clang
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4781230Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4781540Z LLD and LLDB are now provided in separate formulae:
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4782060Z   brew install lld
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4782350Z   brew install lldb
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4782550Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4782860Z Z3 solver support will be removed in LLVM 24 as it is unsupported upstream,
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4783570Z see https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/205370
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4783870Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4784350Z Using `clang`, `clang++`, etc., requires a CLT installation at `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools`.
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4785160Z If you don't want to install the CLT, you can write appropriate configuration files pointing to your
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4785630Z SDK at ~/.config/clang.
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4785800Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4786080Z To use the bundled libunwind please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4786580Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4786820Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4787080Z To use the bundled libc++ please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4788660Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/c++ -L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4789590Z Features newer than system libc++ will require the following define to enable
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4790210Z (support for this may be removed in a future major LLVM release):
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4790720Z   CPPFLAGS="-D_LIBCPP_DISABLE_AVAILABILITY"
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4790970Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4791480Z NOTE: You probably want to use the libunwind and libc++ provided by macOS unless you know what you're doing.
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4791960Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4792310Z llvm is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4792940Z because macOS already provides this software and installing another version in
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4793520Z parallel can cause all kinds of trouble.
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4793760Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4794020Z If you need to have llvm first in your PATH, run:
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4794680Z   echo 'export PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:$PATH"' >> /Users/runner/.bash_profile
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4795040Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4795240Z For compilers to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4795690Z   export LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib"
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4796170Z   export CPPFLAGS="-I/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/include"
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4796450Z 
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4796960Z For cmake to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-10-20T15:22:00.4797500Z   export CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm"
